{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTowerBasicConstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTowerBasicConstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeBraidedCategoryScaffold","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.SimpleModule.Basic"],"declarations":33,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.far_commute_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.far_commute_zero","kind":"theorem","line":397,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L397-L404","doc":"**The obstruction to a finite-rank instance.** `far_commute` forces `σ 0` to\ncommute with every `σ j` for `j ≥ 2` — so the generators past rank cannot be\npadded with a non-commuting real generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.constant_generator_presentation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.constant_generator_presentation","kind":"theorem","line":382,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L382-L395","doc":"**The class is satisfiable — degenerately.** Any single element satisfying\nthe Hecke quadratic yields an instance via the constant family; braid and\nfar-commutation hold by `rfl`.\n\nStated to pin down how weak the class is, not as a recommended instance: nothing\nconditional on a `HeckeBraidedPresentation` obtained this way carries Hecke\ncontent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeMarkovExpectation.markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeMarkovExpectation.markov","kind":"theorem","line":351,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L351-L351","doc":"`ε` collapses the top-generator coset with the Ocneanu scalar `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeMarkovExpectation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeMarkovExpectation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":344,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L344-L344","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeMarkovExpectation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeMarkovExpectation","kind":"class","line":325,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L325-L351","doc":"**§3b DEPENDENT conjecture — the Markov property of the conditional\nexpectation (bean `qou-zm8z`).** GIVEN a conditional expectation, `ε` collapses\nthe `σₙ`-coset with a single scalar:\n\n  `ε (ιlow b · σₙ · ιlow c) = z • (b · c)`.\n\nThis is the defining property of the Markov trace's `z` (the Ocneanu parameter)\nat the level of `ε` rather than of `tr`. `HeckeConditionalExpectation` does NOT\nimply it — that class has exactly `retract` and `bimodule`, neither of which\nsays anything about what `ε` does to the top generator, and `bimodule` in\nparticular only moves `ιlow`-factors across `ε`, leaving `ε σₙ` untouched.\n\n**This class ASSUMES the Markov property; it does not derive it.** Its value is\nthat the assumption is now a named, content-bearing carrier with a stated\ndependency edge, instead of an anonymous hypothesis threaded through call sites\n— and that, combined with `HeckeCosetSpanning`, it is exactly enough to\n*compute* `ε` on an arbitrary element (see\n`MarkovTowerBridge.towerE_eq_of_spanning`). That computation is the new content;\nthe assumption itself is relocated, not discharged. OPEN — no instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeCosetSpanning.spanning","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeCosetSpanning.spanning","kind":"theorem","line":322,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L322-L322","doc":"Every `w : Hn` decomposes over the lower algebra and its `σ k`-coset. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeCosetSpanning.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeCosetSpanning.mk","kind":"ctor","line":317,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L317-L317","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeCosetSpanning","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeCosetSpanning","kind":"class","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L294-L323","doc":"**§3b DEPENDENT conjecture — the coset spanning decomposition (bean\n`qou-zm8z`).** GIVEN the two Hecke braided presentations and the tower\ninclusion `ιlow : Hlow →ₐ Hn`, every element of the larger algebra splits as\n\n  `w = ιlow a + Σᵢ ιlow (b i) · σn n · ιlow (c i)`\n\ni.e. `Hn = Hlow + Hlow · σₙ · Hlow` — the level-`n` algebra is spanned by the\nlower one together with its `σₙ`-double-coset. Classically this is Iwahori's\nbasis theorem / the Coxeter length filtration: a reduced word either avoids the\ntop generator (first summand) or factors through exactly one occurrence of it\n(the sum). Mathlib has neither at general rank, which is why this is a class.\n\n**This is the brick Ocneanu cyclicity induction actually runs on.** The\ninductive step reduces `tr(w₁w₂)` to words of the shape `u·g·v`, and reaching\nan ARBITRARY pair needs exactly this spanning statement to put a general `w`\ninto that shape. Without it the induction is stated only for already-decomposed\nwords. It was named as a deliverable of the W2 re-scope note (bean `qou-2017`)\nalongside `HeckeConditionalExpectation` and `JonesBasicConstruction` and, unlike\nthose two, was never built.\n\nIndependent of the conditional expectation: it mentions neither `ε` nor the\nJones projection, so it can be discharged separately, and a proof of it does not\nneed any trace at all. OPEN — no instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.WenzlTowerStep.semisimple_ascend","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.WenzlTowerStep.semisimple_ascend","kind":"theorem","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L289-L289","doc":"Semisimplicity ascends along a nondegenerate Markov trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.WenzlTowerStep.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.WenzlTowerStep.mk","kind":"ctor","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L284-L284","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.WenzlTowerStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.WenzlTowerStep","kind":"class","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L222-L292","doc":"**§3b DEPENDENT conjecture — the Wenzl tower step (bean `qou-2c4t`,\nthe A1 apex).** GIVEN the presentations, the inclusion, and the Markov\ntrace at level `n+1`, semisimplicity ASCENDS the tower wherever the\ntrace is nondegenerate: if `Hn` is semisimple and `trn1` has no nonzero\nleft kernel, then `Hn1` is semisimple. This is Wenzl's induction step\n[wenzl1988, Thm 2.2]; the proved rungs `isSemisimpleRing_H3A` (and the\nrank-2 `HeckeH2Wedderburn`) realize its conclusion concretely at\n`n = 2, 3` without the tower machinery. Proving this class's field for\nsymmetric-group Coxeter data at the *Markov* trace is the general-`n`\ntarget the explicit-Wedderburn route cannot reach; it is still open.\n\n**Mathlib does not supply the prerequisite; the CORPUS already does (measured\n2026-08-26, bean `qou-kzjl`).** Mathlib's `traceForm_nondegenerate` is\n\n    ∀ (K L) [Field K] [Field L] [Algebra K L] [FiniteDimensional K L]\n      [Algebra.IsSeparable K L], (traceForm K L).Nondegenerate\n\nwhich is wrong here in two independent ways: it runs *separable ⇒ nondegenerate*\nwhere this field needs the converse, and both `K` and `L` are fields where\n`H_n(q)` is non-commutative. Mathlib's `isSemisimpleRing_*` family is structural\n(`iff_jacobson`, `iff_isArtinianRing`, …), none of it trace-form based.\n\nThat Mathlib measurement is correct and is NOT a reason to prove anything new\nhere. The result — *a finite-dimensional algebra over a field with\nnondegenerate regular trace form is semisimple* — has been in this corpus since\nbrick B3d (epic `qou-hnhg`) as\n`QOU.MathlibExt.isSemisimpleRing_of_regTraceForm_nondegenerate`, with its\nnilpotent-trace core in `QOU.MathlibExt.TraceNilpotent`. Recorded because the\ntwo questions are easy to conflate and one of them was: an exhaustive search of\n*Mathlib* says nothing about what the corpus holds.\n\n**What is instantiated, and what is not.**\n`QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.wenzlTowerStep_regTrace` discharges this class's field\nat **general rank** for the *regular* trace `w ↦ trace (L_w)`, so the class is\nno longer instance-free. It contributes an adapter between two spellings of\nnondegeneracy, not a semisimplicity proof. Two things are worth reading off it\nrather than assuming. First, the ascent does not consume the `Hn`-semisimple\nhypothesis at all — nondegeneracy at level `n+1` is the whole of it, which makes\nhypothesis 1 of the field redundant for this trace. Second: the general-`n`\nHecke target needs the field at the **Markov** trace — and that is not merely\nunproved here, it is **false on `H_n` at the canonical convention D**, so no\ninstance of this class at the Markov trace on `H_n` can exist. The convention-D\npin `z(q²+1) = q³` forces the antisymmetric Wedderburn weight `y₍₁³₎` to `0`,\nthat block lies in the radical of the trace form, and `det G = 0` exactly —\n`QOU.QBeta.TemperleyLiebTower.conventionD_kills_antisymmetriser` and\n`QOU.QBeta.MarkovGramDegenerate.gram_det_eq_zero_of_radical_combination`, both\nsorry-free. Independently: the closed-form `n = 3` determinant in\n`gram-matrix-h3-symbolic` carries the factor `(q²+1)z − q³`, which *is* the\nconvention-D pin rearranged, so `det G` vanishes identically in `q` there.\n\nThe Frobenius structure is real but lives on the quotient `H_n / rad τ ≅ TL_n(δ)`\n(`pairing_descends`, `mem_radical_of_pairing_zero`), matching\n`prop:markov-trace-frobenius-selection` (iii). Discharging this class at the\nMarkov trace over that quotient is bean `qou-s7z2`; it is genuine work, since\nboth the braided presentation and the tower inclusion must be restated for the\nquotient. The nearest abstract statement remains\n`QOU.MathlibExt.isSemisimpleRing_of_qGeneric`, which reaches semisimplicity from\n`q`-genericity but takes the Gram–factorial equivalence as a hypothesis, and\nwhose own open input — the general `T_w`-basis determinant, the classical\nSchur-element product formula — is unchanged by any of this.\n\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.JonesBasicConstruction.absorb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.JonesBasicConstruction.absorb","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L218-L218","doc":"Absorption: `e · y · e = ι (ε y) · e` with\n`e = jonesIdempotent q (σn1 n)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.JonesBasicConstruction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.JonesBasicConstruction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L211-L211","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.JonesBasicConstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.JonesBasicConstruction","kind":"class","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L204-L220","doc":"**§3b DEPENDENT conjecture — basic-construction absorption (bean\n`qou-iri6`).** GIVEN a conditional expectation, the level-`n` Jones\nprojection `e = jonesIdempotent q (σn1 n)` absorbs through it:\n`e · y · e = ι (ε y) · e` for every `y : Hn1`. This is the defining\nrelation of the Jones basic construction `⟨Hn1, e⟩`; combined with the\nPROVED local layer (`jonesIdempotent_mul_self` at `σn1 n`) it generates\nthe Temperley–Lieb quotient tower. OPEN — no instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeConditionalExpectation.bimodule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeConditionalExpectation.bimodule","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L202-L202","doc":"`ε` is an `(Hn, Hn)`-bimodule map:\n`ε (ι x * y * ι z) = x * ε y * z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeConditionalExpectation.retract","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeConditionalExpectation.retract","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L199-L199","doc":"`ε` retracts the tower inclusion: `ε (ι x) = x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeConditionalExpectation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeConditionalExpectation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L194-L194","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeConditionalExpectation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeConditionalExpectation","kind":"class","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L185-L202","doc":"**§3b DEPENDENT conjecture — conditional expectation onto the\nsubalgebra (bean `qou-iri6`).** GIVEN the two Hecke braided presentations\nand the tower inclusion `ι : Hn →ₐ Hn1`, an `R`-linear conditional\nexpectation `ε : Hn1 →ₗ Hn`: a retraction of `ι` that is an\n`(Hn, Hn)`-bimodule map. This is the first tower datum of the Jones basic\nconstruction; for Hecke algebras it is classically built from the\nKazhdan–Lusztig/word filtration (`ε` reads off the coefficient layer over\nthe parabolic subalgebra), which is exactly what Mathlib lacks at\ngeneral rank. OPEN — no instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.ofRank_of_unbounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.ofRank_of_unbounded","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L169-L176","doc":"The unbounded class implies the bounded one at every rank — the guards only\ndiscard obligations. So existing consumers lose nothing by moving over. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeBraidedPresentationOfRank.far_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeBraidedPresentationOfRank.far_commute","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L167-L167","doc":"Far commutation, for non-adjacent pairs both present at rank `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeBraidedPresentationOfRank.braid_adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeBraidedPresentationOfRank.braid_adjacent","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L165-L165","doc":"Braid relation, for adjacent pairs both present at rank `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeBraidedPresentationOfRank.hecke_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeBraidedPresentationOfRank.hecke_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L163-L163","doc":"Hecke quadratic, for generators present at rank `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeBraidedPresentationOfRank.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeBraidedPresentationOfRank.mk","kind":"ctor","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L160-L160","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeBraidedPresentationOfRank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.HeckeBraidedPresentationOfRank","kind":"class","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L153-L167","doc":"**Rank-bounded braided presentation.** The three Hecke relations, each\nguarded so it only speaks about generators that exist at rank `n`:\n`σ₀, …, σ_{n-2}` for `H_n`.\n\nCompare `HeckeBraidedCategory.HeckeBraidedPresentation`, whose unguarded `∀ i`\nforces an infinite generator family — the reason it has no contentful instance.\nThe guards here are exactly what makes a finite algebra able to satisfy it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.jonesIdempotent_h2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.jonesIdempotent_h2","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L140-L151","doc":"**Concrete 2×2 slice**: for the diagonal generator\n`σ = diag(q, −q⁻¹)` of `heckeQuadratic_h2`, the Jones projection is\nexactly the antisymmetric-channel projector `diag(0, 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.jonesIdempotent_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.jonesIdempotent_mul","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L127-L138","doc":"Right-hand twin: `e * s = (−q⁻¹) • e`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.mul_jonesIdempotent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.mul_jonesIdempotent","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L119-L125","doc":"The generator acts on its Jones projection by the antisymmetric\neigenvalue: `s * e = (−q⁻¹) • e`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.jonesIdempotent_mul_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.jonesIdempotent_mul_self","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L109-L117","doc":"**The Jones projection is idempotent** — sorry-free, from the Hecke\nquadratic alone, in any `R`-algebra: `e² = e`. This is the proved local\nlayer of the basic construction, valid at every rank simultaneously\n(apply to `s = σᵢ` of any presentation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.sub_sq_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.sub_sq_eq","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L93-L107","doc":"Auxiliary product identity: `(q•1 − s)² = (q+q⁻¹) • (q•1 − s)` under\nthe Hecke quadratic — the unnormalized idempotency, from the channel\nidentity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.mul_sub_channel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.mul_sub_channel","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L82-L91","doc":"**Left eigen-channel identity**: `s · (q•1 − s) = (−q⁻¹) • (q•1 − s)`\n— the unnormalized Jones projection spans the antisymmetric channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.generator_eq_jones","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.generator_eq_jones","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L74-L80","doc":"**Generator recovery**: `s = q•1 − (q+q⁻¹)•e`. Together with\n`jonesIdempotent_mul_self` this exhibits the Hecke algebra's generator\nlayer as the idempotent layer of the basic construction — the standard\nTemperley–Lieb change of generators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.smul_jonesIdempotent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.smul_jonesIdempotent","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L68-L72","doc":"The defining sum: `(q+q⁻¹) • e = q•1 − s`, i.e. the generator is\nrecovered as `s = q•1 − (q+q⁻¹)•e` (`generator_eq_jones`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.jonesIdempotent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.jonesIdempotent","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTowerBasicConstruction.lean#L61-L66","doc":"The **Jones projection** attached to a Hecke generator: the\nnormalized `−q⁻¹`-eigenchannel projector `e = (q+q⁻¹)⁻¹ • (q•1 − s)`.\nDefined for any element of any `R`-algebra; its projection identities\nbelow need only the Hecke quadratic. ","signatureChunk":0}]}